          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాగు — sāgu — \"to go on; to proceed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మా ప్రయాణం హాయిగా సాగింది. mā prayāṇaṁ hāyigā sāgindi. Our journey went on pleasantly."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): సాగాను, sāgānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of a journey, a meeting or a life: సాఫీగా సాగింది, it went smoothly. As a noun సాగు (sāgu) is farming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాగు (sāgu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2430 lists Telugu sāgu, \"to go on, to proceed, to continue\"."
            }
          ]
        },
