              "text": "వెనుదిరుగు — venudirugu — \"to turn back; to head back\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వర్షం వల్ల మేము మధ్యలోనే వెనుదిరిగాం. varṣaṁ valla mēmu madhyalōnē venudirigāṁ. Because of the rain we turned back halfway."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): వెనుదిరిగాను, venudirigānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వెను, back, + తిరుగు, to turn: to turn round and go back the way you came. Said of travellers, and of a side that gives up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వెనుదిరుగు (venudirugu) is native Dravidian: వెను, \"the back\", which DEDR 5488 lists as Telugu ven(n)u beside venuka, \"behind\", and తిరుగు, \"to turn, to go round\" (DEDR 3246), whose త becomes ద inside the compound."
            }
          ]
